# Local 3D Assets

**The user has real GLB models on disk.** Do NOT assume models are missing because search/glob returns empty — `*.glb` files are gitignored but exist locally.

Inventory is in `public/models/MANIFEST.md` and `src/constants/models.ts`.

## Layout (always present locally)

```
public/models/
  drone/drone.glb
  ball/ball.glb
  weapon/ak/ak.glb
  pig/pig.glb              — single skinned pig with all animation clips
  shelter/shelter.glb      — bunker (replaces the box placeholder)
  rat/rat.glb              — skinned rats inside shelters (Walking, Fall_Dead_from_Abdominal_Injury)
  trees/*.glb, crate/, granit/, dirt/, damaged-wall/, terrain/ — Outskirts dressing
```

Legacy per-clip pig GLBs may still exist on disk but are **not used** — all clips are in `pig.glb`.

## Pig animations

Clip names are mapped in `PIG_CLIPS` (`src/constants/models.ts`). Current `pig.glb` clips: `Walking`, `Running`, `Walk_Backward_While_Shooting`, `Leap_Right_and_Catch`, `Dead`. Inspect clips:

```bash
npx @gltf-transform/cli inspect public/models/pig/pig.glb
```

Walk/run are **in-place**. World travel is in `update-soldiers.ts`; face walk direction in `pig-soldier.tsx`. Use `PigAnimatedModel` with crossfade — `SkeletonUtils.clone` + `useAnimations(animations, cloneRef)` on the cloned Object3D. Fit with `updateMatrixWorld(true)` and `PIG_TARGET_HEIGHT` (~1.65m); the Armature is scaled 0.01.

## Drone model

- Path: `drone/drone.glb` — config in `DRONE_MODEL` (`src/constants/models.ts`).
- **Blender axes (raw GLB):** forward **−Y**, up **+Z**; rugby mesh on the **rear**, not the nose.
- **Game:** Y-up, path on XZ, physics yaw on world Y, forward `droneForwardVector` (−Z at yaw 0).
- **Loading:** `StaticModel` applies `DRONE_MODEL.rotation` + `targetSize` fit; `drone.tsx` sets `rotation.y = −drone.yaw` (smoothed).
- **Camera:** `FpvCamera` tracks `droneForwardVector` — keep mesh/camera/physics in sync; do not reintroduce extra Euler flips on the GLB without testing.
- **Propellers:** four corner meshes (`Meshy_Meshy_Model_mesh_node*`). `isDronePropellerNode` in `models.ts`; `drone-model.tsx` spins them around local Y. Fallback: meshes offset from the body in XZ.

## Agent tooling

- Use shell `Get-ChildItem public/models -Recurse` to list files when glob fails.
- Never replace GLB models with placeholders unless the user asks.
